        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Set amid one of County Sligos most sought-after coastal enclaves, this exceptional site extending to approximately 1.16 acres offers a rare opportunity to acquire a truly special piece of shoreline at Ballyweelin, Rosses Point.\r\n\r\nEnjoying direct access to its own private stretch of coastline, the property commands breathtaking, uninterrupted views across Sligo Bay towards the iconic silhouette of Knocknarea. The ever-changing seascape, coupled with the dramatic backdrop of mountain and sky, creates a setting of outstanding natural beauty.\r\n\r\nKey Features:\r\n\r\nGenerous site extending to circa 1.16 acres\r\n\r\nExclusive private shoreline access\r\n\r\nSpectacular views across Sligo Bay to Knocknarea\r\n\r\nPrime location between Rosses Point and Sligo Town\r\n\r\nPeaceful yet highly accessible setting.\r\n\r\nExceptional opportunity to create a bespoke coastal home\r\n\r\nThis is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to secure a landmark coastal site in an area of outstanding natural beauty, where privacy, scenery and convenience come together in perfect harmony.\r\n\r\nLocation\r\nPerfectly positioned between the vibrant seaside village of Rosses Point and the bustling heart of Sligo Town, the location offers the ideal balance of seclusion and convenience. Rosses Point, just minutes away, is renowned for its sandy beaches, championship golf links, yacht club and welcoming coastal atmosphere, while Sligo Town (approx. 10 minutes drive) provides a full range of amenities including schools, shops, restaurants and cultural attractions.\r\n\r\nDirections: These lands are situated just 1km from Rosses Point Village, just off the R291."
      }
    ],
